.TH "idevicepcap" 1
.SH NAME
idevicepcap \- Capture network traffic from a device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B idevicepcap
[OPTIONS]

.SH DESCRIPTION

Capture network traffic from an iOS device using the device's
.B com.apple.pcapd
service. The device must be paired with this host. Each captured packet includes
the process that owns the socket; this metadata is stored as a packet comment in
PCAPNG output and is printed to standard error while capturing.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-udid UDID
Target specific device by UDID.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-network
Connect to network device.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output FILE
Write captured packets to FILE. The default is
.B capture.pcapng.
Use
.B -
to write to standard output.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-format FORMAT
Select the output format:
.B pcapng
(default) or
.B pcap.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-count N
Stop after N captured packets. The default is unlimited; press CTRL+C to stop.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-process NAME|PID
Only capture packets owned by this process, or by this process ID. Both the
socket-owning process and the effective process are matched.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interface NAME
Only capture packets on this interface. Use the full name such as
.B en0,
or the interface name without its unit such as
.B en
to match every unit.
.TP
.B \-P, \-\-pair
Validate or create the host pairing before capture. If the device has not been
paired yet, accept the trust dialog on the device.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Do not print a one-line packet summary on standard error.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable communication debugging.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Prints usage information.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Prints version information.

.SH NOTES

The device must be unlocked and trusted by this host. Traffic from interfaces
without a link-layer header is given a synthetic Ethernet header so the capture
can be opened by standard tools such as Wireshark and tshark.

.SH ON THE WEB
https://libimobiledevice.org

https://github.com/libimobiledevice/libimobiledevice
